# The build context is the repository root: server and bot share common/, so narrowing the context to each service's directory would put common/ out of reach of COPY. That means the whole root is sent, so anything that must not end up in the image is dropped here.

# Local-only notes, already gitignored. No reason to ship them in the image.
local/

# History. Not needed in the image, inflates the context transfer, and would hand over any credentials contained in past commits.
.git/
.gitignore

# Config is mounted at runtime, never baked into the image. Baking it in would leave the DB password, the Discord bot token and the OAuth2 client secret in an image layer, so distributing the image distributes the credentials with it; deleting the layer does not help, because the credentials stay recoverable from the image history.
config.yaml

# The environment-variable file docker compose reads. It holds the DB password, so it is excluded for the same reason as config.yaml.
.env

# Python bytecode built on the host. The container's Python may be a different version from the host's, so carrying the bytecode in means the container loads broken .pyc files.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Host virtualenv. Container dependencies are installed from requirements.txt when the image is built.
.venv/
venv/

# Runtime artifacts.
*.log
*.db
